From: johnnykang101 <56775858+johnnykang101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Mar 2026 09:34:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 091/131] =?UTF-8?q?fix(cd):=20npm-install=20electron-vite+?=
 =?UTF-8?q?picocolors=20directly=20on=20Windows=20=E2=80=94=20no=20catalog?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20juggling=20(#35)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bun's symlink linker breaks on Windows (symlinks need elevated permissions),
causing electron-vite to fail finding picocolors at runtime. Instead of
manipulating package.json to resolve catalog: entries, just npm-install
electron-vite and picocolors directly with --no-save. bun install still
handles all workspace: deps; npx then uses the flat npm copy of electron-vite.

Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .github/workflows/cd.yml | 27 ++++++---------------------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/cd.yml b/.github/workflows/cd.yml
index f69a3f1f3..2b07718fd 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/cd.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/cd.yml
@@ -292,27 +292,12 @@ jobs:
             fs.writeFileSync('package.json', JSON.stringify(pkg, null, 2) + '\n');
           "
 
-      # Bun runs electron-vite from an isolated .bun cache dir that lacks
-      # peer deps (picocolors) on Windows. Use npm+npx instead.
-      # catalog: entries must be resolved first since npm doesn't understand them.
-      - name: Resolve catalog deps and install with npm (Windows)
-        shell: pwsh
-        run: |
-          $catalog = (Get-Content package.json | ConvertFrom-Json).catalog
-          $pkg = Get-Content packages/desktop-electron/package.json | ConvertFrom-Json
-          foreach ($section in @("dependencies","devDependencies")) {
-            $deps = $pkg.$section
-            if (-not $deps) { continue }
-            $deps.PSObject.Properties | ForEach-Object {
-              if ($_.Value -eq "catalog:") {
-                $resolved = $catalog.($_.Name)
-                if ($resolved) { $deps.($_.Name) = $resolved }
-              }
-            }
-          }
-          $pkg | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 10 | Set-Content packages/desktop-electron/package.json
-          cd packages/desktop-electron
-          npm install --legacy-peer-deps
+      # Bun resolves electron-vite through its symlink linker, which breaks on
+      # Windows (symlinks require elevated permissions). Fix: npm-install just
+      # electron-vite + picocolors so npx uses a flat, working copy. No need to
+      # touch package.json or resolve catalog: entries.
+      - name: Install electron-vite with npm (Windows symlink fix)
+        run: cd packages/desktop-electron && npm install electron-vite picocolors --no-save --legacy-peer-deps
 
       - name: Build
         run: cd packages/desktop-electron && npx electron-vite build
